{
  "name": "SL_Test_Scenarios",
  "description": "Leg-level Stop Loss test matrix: one leg per (SL type x on_sl_action) combination. SL types = percentage / points / trailing / atr (the 'none' type is excluded because it disables SL and cannot represent an SL condition). on_sl_action = close / re_execute / reverse / execute / re_entry / keep_leg_running. 4 x 6 = 24 scenario legs + 1 shared disarmed 'exec_target' leg that the 4 execute legs arm via execute_target_leg_id. PORTFOLIO-LEVEL SL is ON (pf_sl_type='Combined Loss', pf_sl_action='SqOff'): when the combined PnL across all legs breaches pf_sl_value (2% of starting_capital = 6000), EVERY leg in the portfolio is squared off (both sqoff_only_loss_legs and sqoff_only_profit_legs are false, so all legs close, not just losers/winners). Note: '*__keep_leg_running' computes the leg SL but never acts on it (expected) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the portfolio-level SqOff still closes those legs.",
